  "response": "Coordinated with `opus` via `/work/board.md` and verified `/work/answer.md`.\n\n- **Exact condition (for $v_A, v_B, v_C > 0$ and $v_A + v_B + v_C > v_P \\ge 0$):** The Vickrey-nearest core point equals the centroid of the minimum-revenue face $F$ if and only if:\n  1. $v_P \\le \\min(v_A, v_B, v_C)$, or\n  2. $v_P \\ge v_i + v_j$ for all pairs $i \\ne j$ (equivalently, $v_P + \\min(v_A, v_B, v_C) \\ge v_A + v_B + v_C$), or\n  3. $v_A = v_B = v_C$.\n- **Counterexample:** For $v_P = 4$ and $(v_A, v_B, v_C) = (2, 3, 4)$, the Vickrey-nearest point is $(4/3, 4/3, 4/3)$ while the centroid of $F$ is $(31/33, 46/33, 5/3)$.",
